From 74fbbba89407bef89224f70b7da0b719bb7832ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aliaksei Kandratsenka <alkondratenko@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:47:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] rfc:elf: prototype of dl_events_subscribe for glibc

See https://tinyurl.com/dl-events-subscribe-design for the API design
doc.

Note, this is work-in-progress/RFC. No tests are added yet and
documentation has not been updated.

Here are the glibc-specific details of the prototype implementation.
We hook into the same update points that are currently used by
_dl_find_object, and the actual dl_events_subscribe implementation
lives in the same file (dl-find_object.c). The implementation is
mostly straightforward. We keep a linked list of all subscriptions
and a per-module list of the subscriptions tied to that module. The
new _dl_find_object_pre_dlclose call is where a module's
subscriptions are dropped. The mutation ban (callbacks may not call
dlopen, dlclose or dl_events_subscribe) is implemented with the
dl_mutations_forbidden flag, protected by dl_load_lock. The existing
_dl_find_object_update and _dl_find_object_dlclose calls are where
subscription callbacks are invoked.

There is also a new _dl_find_object_note_dl_fini call, invoked from
_dl_fini, that drops existing subscriptions and disables all future
ones.

Signed-off-by: Aliaksei Kandratsenka <alkondratenko@gmail.com>
