 extern int dl_iterate_phdr (int (*__callback) (struct dl_phdr_info *,
 					       size_t, void *),
 			    void *__data);
 
+/* dl_events_subscribe installs a subscription for module load and
+   unload events.  The C library invokes __CALLBACK with a struct
+   dl_phdr_info, as dl_iterate_phdr does, except that dlpi_adds and
+   dlpi_subs are set to 0.  __IS_UNLOAD is 1 for unload events and 0
+   for load events.  The dl_phdr_info data is valid only for the
+   duration of the callback.
+
+   __CALLBACK may be invoked with internal dynamic linker locks held.
+   It must not call functions that load or unload modules (such as
+   dlopen, dlclose or dl_events_subscribe), or anything that may call
+   them indirectly (e.g. iconv or NSS functions); such calls fail.  It
+   must also not wait for other threads that may be performing such
+   operations.  __CALLBACK must return normally; it must not exit via
+   longjmp or by throwing an exception.
+
+   Callback invocations are not guaranteed to be serialized: different
+   threads may invoke callbacks for different events concurrently, so
+   there is no single global order of events.  It is only guaranteed
+   that:
+
+   a) dl_events_subscribe invokes __CALLBACK for all currently loaded
+      modules before it returns;
+
+   b) dlopen invokes all registered callbacks for each newly loaded
+      module before the module's constructors run;
+
+   c) dlclose invokes all registered callbacks for each unloaded
+      module after the destructors of all unloaded modules have run,
+      and before the module is unmapped.
+
+   Unload events may occasionally be reported without a prior load
+   event, and duplicate load events may be reported, but a load event
+   for a module is never reported after its matching unload event.
+   The order in which registered callbacks are invoked for an event is
+   unspecified.  Whether the module being reported is visible to other
+   dynamic linker query interfaces (such as _dl_find_object, dladdr or
+   dl_iterate_phdr) while __CALLBACK runs is also unspecified.
+
+   There is no dl_events_unsubscribe.  A subscription is associated
+   with the module that contains __CALLBACK and is canceled when that
+   module is unloaded by dlclose, before its destructors run; __DATA
+   must remain valid until then.  If __CALLBACK is not part of any
+   module (e.g. generated code), the subscription is only canceled at
+   process exit.  If dl_events_subscribe is called after the
+   unloading of __CALLBACK's module has started (for example, from
+   that module's destructor), __CALLBACK is still invoked for all
+   currently loaded modules, but no subscription is established.
+
+   At process exit, all subscriptions are canceled when the dynamic
+   linker's exit processing starts.  This happens after exit handlers
+   registered from the main program's constructors onwards (including
+   atexit handlers and C++ static destructors of the main program and
+   of dlopen'ed modules), but before any ELF destructors run and
+   before exit handlers registered by the constructors of initially
+   loaded shared objects (such as their C++ static destructors).
+   Callback state must remain valid until then.  No unload events are
+   reported at exit.  Calls made after process exit has started still
+   invoke __CALLBACK for all currently loaded modules, but establish
+   no subscription.  In statically linked programs, subscriptions are
+   not canceled at exit.
+
+   Unlike dl_iterate_phdr, and like _dl_find_object, this interface
+   reports events for all dynamic linker namespaces.
+
+   Returns 0 on success, or an error number on failure (errno is not
+   set): ENOMEM if memory for the subscription could not be
+   allocated, or EDEADLK if called from a dl_events_subscribe
+   callback.  */
+extern int dl_events_subscribe (void (*__callback) (struct dl_phdr_info *__info,
+						    size_t __info_size,
+						    void *__data,
+						    int __is_unload),
+				void *__data);
 
